## 6. Security Threat Model (STRIDE Framework)

```
+-------------------+-------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+
| Threat Category   | Identified Risk                     | Architectural Mitigation                             |
+-------------------+-------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+
| Spoofing          | Forged initData or impersonated     | Server-side HMAC-SHA256 signature check using Bot     |
|                   | user requests.                      | Token secret; client-supplied User ID is ignored.     |
+-------------------+-------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+
| Tampering         | Client alters purchase amount or    | Server maintains authoritative plan pricing. Client    |
|                   | subscription duration in payload.   | only sends plan_id; backend sets invoice amount.       |
+-------------------+-------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+
| Repudiation       | Unauthorized admin changes or       | Immutable append-only `audit_logs` table capturing    |
|                   | manual user unblocking.             | admin ID, entity ID, diff changes, and IP address.    |
+-------------------+-------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+
| Information       | Sensitive database errors or bot    | Error-handling middleware returns generic JSON response;|
| Disclosure        | tokens exposed in API errors.       | secrets loaded exclusively via runtime environment.   |
+-------------------+-------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+
| Denial of Service | API endpoint flooding or notification| Redis-backed Token Bucket rate limiting on API routers;|
|                   | queue overload.                     | async background workers process tasks off main thread|
+-------------------+-------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+
| Elevation of      | Non-admin user querying admin APIs  | Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) middleware validating |
| Privilege         | via direct URL access (IDOR).       | token claims and DB role on every protected request.  |
+-------------------+-------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+

```

